C/Panako/Kdenlive output, and no v2 execution entered it.","rerun_contract":{"cases":"every benchmark case eligible for gcc_phat_argmax_v1 (24 positive + 24 wrong-reference + 2 repeats)","inputs":"hash-verified trimmed inputs and references, loaded identically to the frozen run (float64, mean of channels, native 48 kHz)","outputs":{"raw_assembly":"experiments\\applied_system\\final_pack\\results\\gcc_phat_v2_lagfix_raw.json","records_dir":"experiments\\applied_system\\final_pack\\results\\gcc_phat_v2_lagfix_records","scored_results":"experiments\\applied_system\\final_pack\\results\\gcc_phat_v2_lagfix_results.json"},"scoring":"frozen scoring.py contract; 100 ms primary, 50/150 ms sensitivity; no new threshold","semantics":"ALWAYS_OUTPUT argmax; no threshold, no refusal, no no-match detector","v1_evidence":"preserved verbatim; nothing under final_comparator_raw_records/ or any frozen artifact is modified"},"root_cause":"gcc_phat_runner.curve_argmax_offset_samples unwraps the zero-padded FFT correlation at the length-independent midpoint ceil(N/2). Linear-correlation lag support depends on BOTH lengths: negative lags occupy indices N-Ly+1..N-1. When the query is shorter than the reference (N close to Lx+Ly), part of the negative-lag support lies below the midpoint and v1 reports it as a positive lag larger by exactly N samples; when the query is longer, part of the positive support is reported negative by N. Equal lengths are unaffected.","sign_convention":"lag m means y_rec[n] ~= y_ref[n - m]; the reference begins m samples into the capture; identical to the production engine and the frozen ground truth (gt = payload_start_in_trimmed - slice_start)","synthetic_validation":{"fixture_families":["impulse pairs over {query shorter, equal, query longer} x {zero, positive, negative, both single-sample boundary} lags","exact delayed-copy broadband pairs (pure linear phase -> exact PHAT delta) at deep negative and large positive lags in both misread regions","noise-added delayed copy (deterministic seed)","full lag sweep (stride 37) over an unequal pair, v1 correct iff outside the misread region","sign-convention, determinism, file-contract, and NCC-unaffected checks"],"independent_reference":"direct linear cross-correlation (scipy.signal.correlate, direct method) with explicit lag axis","result":"26 passed (run before any final-case re-execution)","test_module":"experiments/applied_system/tests/test_gcc_phat_lagfix.py"},"system_v1":"gcc_phat_argmax_v1","system_v2":"gcc_phat_argmax_v2_lagfix","verdict":"GCC_LAG_MAPPING_BUG_CONFIRMED"},"freeze_hash":"a93c9c3e3923203521d4382bb5d751c718728d423819c38672758ea7ef8dae50"}
